{"symbol":"MCI.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:53:11Z","info":{"address1":"Warsaw Unit","address2":"Rondo Ignacego Daszynskiego 1","city":"Warsaw","zip":"00-843","country":"Poland","phone":"48 22 540 7380","fax":"48 22 540 7381","website":"https://www.mci.pl/en","industry":"Asset Management","industryKey":"asset-management","industryDisp":"Asset Management","sector":"Financial Services","sectorKey":"financial-services","sectorDisp":"Financial Services","longBusinessSummary":"MCI Capital Alternatywna Spólka Inwestycyjna S.A., is a private equity and venture capital firm specializing in seed/startup, early to late venture, buy-out, middle market, mature, emerging growth, and growth capital investments. The firm seeks to invest in digital economy, digital climatech with a focus in area of green transformation in technology/digital companies, digital disruption, digital transformation & digital infrastructure. Preferred sectors are SaaS, e-commerce, payments, marketplace, security, fintech, proptech, food, travel, insurtech, foodtech, deeptech, Internet infrastructure like fibre and 5G, telecoms, IoT, traveltech, B2C apps, consumer discretionary, consumer services, logistics infrastructure, retailing, financials, insurance, information technology, software, communication services, media, entertainment, Healthcare & Longevity, D2C, AI & Digital Native. It seeks to invest in Israel, Africa/Middle East, Nordic countries (Denmark, Finland, Iceland, Norway, Sweden), across Central and Eastern Europe (Developed & Emerging Markets) with a focus on North CEE (Poland, Baltics, Czech Republic, Slovakia, Hungary), South CEE (Romania, Bulgaria, Slovenia, Croatia, Greece) and DACH countries (Germany, Austria, Switzerland, Italy). The firm prefers to invest between 25 million ($26.97 million) and 100 million ($107.90 million). The firm prefers to take majority stake. It has also been historically involved in funds dedicated to Private Debt, Growth and Venture Capital areas. MCI Capital Alternatywna Spólka Inwestycyjna S.A. was founded in 1999 and is based in Warsaw, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":19,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Tomasz Janusz Czechowicz","age":55,"title":"Founder, CEO, Chairman of Mgmt Board, Managing Partner, Chief Investment Officer & Fund Manager","yearBorn":1970,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Ewa  Ogryczak","title":"VP, COO, Senior Partner & Vice Chairman of the Management Board","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Pawel  Borys","title":"Managing Partner, Chief Investment Officer & Vice President of the Management Board","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Aleksandra  Kulas","title":"Chief Financial Officer","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Katarzyna  Pogorzelska","title":"Treasury & Operations Director","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Marcin  Nowohonski","title":"Head of Valuation & Portfolio Controlling","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Filip  Berkowski","title":"Executive Partner","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Michal  Gorecki","title":"Senior Investment Partner","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Milena  Sikorska","title":"Risk Officer & Fund Controller","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Pawel  Sikorski","title":"Investment Partner","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0}],"executiveTeam":[],"maxAge":86400,"priceHint":2,"previousClose":27.4,"open":27.5,"dayLow":27.5,"dayHigh":28,"regularMarketPreviousClose":27.4,"regularMarketOpen":27.5,"regularMarketDayLow":27.5,"regularMarketDayHigh":28,"dividendRate":1.58,"dividendYield":5.77,"exDividendDate":1789603200,"payoutRatio":1.7889,"beta":0.484,"trailingPE":31.1111,"volume":5592,"regularMarketVolume":5592,"averageVolume":5032,"averageVolume10days":4465,"averageDailyVolu